Sval: draw an SVG image with the site style of the page showing it

An SVG image is a document of its own with no BrowsingContext, so it would
keep its colors while the page around it is tinted or dark. The page's
style travels in the SVGImageContext, which keys the image's cached
renderings, and the image's pres context paints with it.

